# Ownership
#
# One owner: @princeofscale. There is no GitHub organization behind this repository
# yet, and GitHub teams only exist inside an organization, so a per-role team handle
# would be a name that resolves to nothing — which reads as a review requirement and
# enforces none. A single real account is honest: GitHub can require review by it,
# and `docs/development/release-readiness.md` tracks that requirement as an open
# external gate until branch protection is turned on.
#
# The role distinction that mattered under placeholder handles — which paths are
# security-sensitive and which are engine-sensitive — is not lost. It lives in
# `SECURITY.md`, which states the criterion and the list, and
# `tools/ci/test_ci_checks.py` checks that this file and that one agree in both
# directions and that every path named in either exists in the tree.

