## What this file does and does not do

Every path listed as security-sensitive in `SECURITY.md` is owned here, and every
path named in either file exists in the tree. `tools/ci/test_ci_checks.py` checks
both directions, so a security-sensitive path with no owner, and a path that is
listed but is not in the tree, are each a failure.

The criterion for the list is written down in `SECURITY.md`.

That sentence is here because `tools/ci/test_ci_checks.py` checks for it: an ownership
file and a security policy that describe the same paths have to say so in the same
words, or one of them drifts and nothing notices.

What this file does not do is enforce anything on its own. `CODEOWNERS` is inert
until branch protection requires a review, and no ruleset requires one yet: the only
possible reviewer is the repository owner, so a self-review would satisfy the
requirement without adding a second pair of eyes. That is an open external gate in
`docs/development/release-readiness.md`, listed as gate 7, and it is the reason the
next thing this project needs is a second maintainer rather than another test.
